    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[TrustedTypes: SVGAnimatedString.baseVal]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42502</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42502"/>
        <updated>2025-12-23T05:59:14.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">The <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/SVGAnimatedString" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">SVGAnimatedString</code></a> can represent the base and animated values of various elements in SVG.</p>
<p dir="auto">In the context of <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/SVGScriptElement/href" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">SVGScriptElement.href</code></a> it can be used to set the <code class="notranslate">baseVal</code> of the script. This is an injection sink.</p>
<p dir="auto">Technically right place for all the information is  <code class="notranslate">SVGAnimatedString.baseVal</code> since that defines the property, but that can be used to reflect numerous attributes, and only one is a problem case. So what I have done is put TT info in the <code class="notranslate">SVGScriptElement.href</code>. For  <code class="notranslate">SVGAnimatedString.baseVal</code> I have put the disclaimer and explanation, but I link to the other doc for security considerations and the example.</p>
<p dir="auto">Related docs work tracked in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3510273732" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41507" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/41507/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41507">#41507</a></p>]]></content>
